# Units that open /etc/substrate/private AT RUNTIME and therefore override the
# default-deny drop-in service.d/05-secret-dir-out-of-reach.conf with a same-named
# file in their own <unit>.service.d/. One list; nothing implicit. (systemd reads only
# *.conf in a drop-in directory, so this file configures nothing.)
# Read by validation/scripts/secret-dir-mask.test.sh: every entry has its override,
# every override has its entry. A unit that only LOADS a secret (EnvironmentFile=)
# needs no exemption and must not have one.
# Format: <unit> <reason>
identity-seeder.service      seed-identity writes the minted SUBSTRATE_ADMIN_KEY into private/admin.env and its consumers' private/env.d files
substrate-pull-sync.service  renders, migrates and retires the scoped files (render-secret-scope), writes them on vessel-ctl install, and runs secret-mask-probe check, which must stat the real files
